"""Synthetic gold set, part D: Escalation and Hostility (full-call criteria, batch B3).

Labels are BY CONSTRUCTION, NOT human-verified. Item = (label, hard, payload).
Payload = list of lines "Customer: ..." / "Agent: ..." (a short complete call).

The default qa-analysis criteria do not define these two items, so the descriptions used for the Ollama
baseline are written here (EXPLICIT ASSUMPTION), in the same VIOLATION-BASED style as the repo's other items.
They live in run_eval.py (CRITERION_DEFS).

ESCALATION: FAIL = the customer asks for a supervisor, manager or escalation and the agent refuses,
ignores, discourages or fakes it. PASS = no request was made, or the request was handled properly.
HOSTILITY: FAIL = the agent is hostile, abusive, insulting, threatening, mocking, or hangs up on the
customer. PASS = the agent stays professional, even when the customer is angry or abusive.
"""

